  "citation": "NEC-5 printouts captured as End-User Reports; NEC-5 is (c) LLNL, LLNL-CODE-746721. The binary is user-licensed and never distributed. Decks were emitted by EZNEC Pro/2+ v7.0.4 driving NEC5CL_x13.exe (antennaknobs capture sessions, momwire#390/#456); printouts are the Windows engine\u2019s own, byte-verbatim including CRLF line endings.",
  "source": "antennaknobs scratch/eznec-capture/ (capture ids preserved); scored matrix: antennaknobs docs/status/2026-08-20-eznec-nec5-scored-matrix.md",
  "normalizations": "byte-compare after: CRLF->LF; drop FILL=/RUN TIME timing lines; normalize -0.00 vs 0.00 signed zero in pattern TILT columns; drop every SOMMPD.NEX cache block, each of which is ONE BLANK LINE followed by a run of cache lines (the blank is part of the block; dropping it leaves the finite-ground ANTENNA ENVIRONMENT block the same heading/blank/name shape FREE SPACE and PERFECT GROUND already have). Four block forms are observed across these captures: STALE, ' GMPINO: EPSC from file = <epsc>' + '              should be  <epsc>' + ' Will compute Sommerfeld-ground tables' (0021/0047/0048); VALID, 'Sommerfeld integral tables read:' + 'Potentials: 11 12 13 14 15' + 'E, H:' (0022); ABSENT, ' GMPINO: Unable to open file SOMMPD.NEX' (blank-padded to 70 columns) + ' Will compute Sommerfeld-ground tables' (measured on the linux oracle 2026-08-20, no capture); and the POSTAMBLE all four print between the EN echo and RUN TIME, 'Sommerfeld integral tables written in previous run:' + 'Potentials: 11 12 13 14 15' + 'E and H:' (0022 writes 'E and H: 11 12 13 14 15'). The seam never reads and never writes SOMMPD.NEX, so it emits none of them.",
